  "question": {
    "text": "Which of the following is the correct order of decreasing $\\mathrm{SN}^2$ reactivity?"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "\n$\\mathrm{RCH}_2 \\mathrm{X}>\\mathrm{R}_3 \\mathrm{CX}>\\mathrm{R}_2 \\mathrm{CHX}$\n",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "\n$\\mathrm{RCH}_2 \\mathrm{X}>\\mathrm{R}_2 \\mathrm{CHX}>\\mathrm{R}_3 \\mathrm{CX}$\n",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "\n$\\mathrm{R}_3 \\mathrm{CX}>\\mathrm{R}_2 \\mathrm{CHX}>\\mathrm{RCH}_2 X$\n",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "\n$\\mathrm{R}_2 \\mathrm{CHX}>\\mathrm{R}_3 \\mathrm{CX}>\\mathrm{RCH}_2 \\mathrm{X}$ \n$(\\mathrm{X}=$ a halogen $)$",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "B"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "More is the steric hindrance at the carbon bearing the halogen, lesser is the $\\mathrm{S}_{\\mathrm{N}} 2$ reactivity. \nHence, (B) is correct."
  }
}